clude `evidence` (path:line), `quote` (exact code), and `note` (paths\nsearched and why the condition holds or fails) at the top level of your verdict.\nIf present, evaluate the checks below: a failed control makes this a gap; if you\ncannot show a failed control, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\nIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n\n\n## R04.1\n\n**Check:** Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/loop.ts:51 — \"const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** There is no index, so no write path exists to check.\n\n`src/agent/loop.ts` lines 39–63 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  39      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n  40  \n  41      const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n  42      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n  43      if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n  44      if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n  45        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n  46        return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n  47      }\n  48  \n  49      const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n  50      const tools = registry.definitions();\n  51>     const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = 